BlitzMax.Format formats BlitzMax source text using the syntax model in
#BlitzMax.Language. It does not depend on the language server or an editor.

Create a #TBlitzMaxFormatOptions object to select formatting rules. A new
options object contains the defaults. Pass it to #TBlitzMaxFormatter.FormatText
to receive formatted text, or call #TBlitzMaxFormatter.Query to receive
#TBlitzMaxFormatEdits for an editor or another tool to apply.

Edit start and finish positions are offsets into the original BlitzMax String.
Call #TBlitzMaxFormatEdits.Apply to apply all returned edits safely. Protocol
clients can convert these offsets to their own position encoding.

If the parser reports syntax errors, the formatter returns no edits and
FormatText returns the source unchanged. Multiline string contents and other
protected source regions retain their layout.
